#!/bin/bash
# Test stand-in for any command a hook runs (vaultmind, date, ...). A test
# links a command name to this file and writes the behaviour to <link>.body,
# which is sourced here rather than executed.
#
# Why: macOS scans every newly written executable before its first run - up to
# four minutes each on a loaded machine (#191). One stub per test paid that
# every time; this committed file is scanned once, and a body is never exec.
. "$0.body"
